Based on the analysis of the provided scene images, here is the semantic interpretation grounded in the ontology vocabulary.

### Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)

```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "Dog Running on the Road at Night" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :BehaviorAnomaly ;
    :hasActor :dog1 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :nightWeather ;
    :hasRisk :risk1 .

:dog1 a :Actor ;
    a :Obstacle ; # Assuming the dog is considered an obstacle in this context.

:nightWeather a :NightCondition .

:risk1 a :CollisionRisk ;
    a :PedestrianCollisionRisk ;
    :description "Risk of collision with a dog running across the road" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.75"^^xsd:float .
```

### Identified Risks for each risk class

